      <PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>Our mission is to promote the love of tennis among all ages and backgrounds with a special focus on nurturing young athletes to become lifelong tennis players with skills in dedication, discipline, and resilience.</PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Our club programs achieved various accomplishments, including fostering healthy competition among the community, providing diverse tennis training opportunities, and developing player skills across all levels and ages. The club aims to promote the sport of tennis, create lasting friendships, and even developed a few college players. The After School Program, Summer Camp, Team Tennis and Family Tennis Day served over 400 participants during the year. These free and/or low cost programs extends throughout various backgrounds and ethnicity focusing on under resourced neighborhoods. Last year, there were 5 adult teams who won there way to Southern Cal sectionals. Also, we are proud of the our high school team Home of the Morse High School Mighty Tigers finished up third place in the ITF State wide conference. As a result of being able to showcase their skills, 3 of the team members were invited to college campuses for college recruitment. We raised over 10k through two fundraisers with members and friends. We held 21 tournaments, hosted 19 Adult teams and 3 Junior team tennis events. We collaborated with United States Tennis Association USTA to offer junior scholarships to 4 junior players. The scholarships were designed to assist with tennis clinics, junior tournament fees and travel expenses. We are confident that by offering a positive club culture, we will continue to see growth in all aspect of our operation.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
